&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a resourceful, proactive, and detail-oriented Executive Assistant to support one Vice President across our UK business organisation. In this role, you’ll help leaders operate effectively by managing calendars, coordinating travel and events, supporting meeting preparation, and maintaining strong documentation and record-keeping practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with teams in the UK and internationally, including the Affirm Leadership Support Team, and cross-functional partners across the business. You’ll report directly to the VP, Country Manager UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide high-quality administrative support to one Vice President&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage inboxes, calendars, scheduling, and meeting prioritisation to help leaders use their time effectively&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Co-ordinate core meetings in the daily / weekly / monthly operating plan, ensuring attendance, drafting and distributing agendas, preparing materials, creating decks / notion pages, communicating with attendees and ensuring follow up actions are&amp;nbsp; shared in a timely manner and tracked to completion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage incoming correspondence, including email and physical mail, and coordinate timely intake and forwarding from the managed office facility&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure VP is fully prepared for all core meetings that they attend linking all relevant documentation into calendar invites and providing timely reminders, blocking off time in diaries to ensure sufficient preparation and review time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Co-ordinate team events, team-building activities, and onsite/offsite meetings in various locations, including travel as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure monthly in-office days are planned and well attended, including booking office space, organising food and refreshments, ensuring AV equipment is available and operational.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Plan and co-ordinate all travel for VP in good time ensuring tracking, monitoring and communication of any delays , cancellations and changes to travel plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support&amp;nbsp; and complete expense reporting and travel coordination through Navan travel system&lt;/p&gt;
