&lt;p&gt;As a global team, we embrace collaboration, continuous improvement, and operational excellence. We leverage technology, standardized processes, and strong governance practices to manage the complexities of international payroll while supporting a diverse and growing workforce. Our commitment to accuracy, confidentiality, and customer service enables us to provide reliable payroll solutions that support both employees and business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining our Global Payroll Team means becoming part of a dynamic, fast-paced environment where your expertise will directly contribute to employee satisfaction, regulatory compliance, and the success of our global operations. We value innovation, attention to detail, and a proactive mindset, empowering team members to drive process improvements and make a meaningful impact on a worldwide scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will be reporting to the Senior Manager, Global Payroll.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with the People Platform, Benefits, Legal, and Finance business units on all payroll matters with cross-functional impact such as accurate benefit information, new joiner processes, cash, bonus, process leavers, and other ad hoc projects impacting payroll.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Process U.K. and Spain payroll.&amp;nbsp; This role will grow with additional EU countries under our high growth model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assist with processing RSUs and ESPP earnings and taxation.&lt;/p&gt;
