&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Affirm&#39;s engineering team is building a large-scale, highly available, and global infrastructure that is shared across multiple financial products. Ensuring that our infrastructure is accessible to all engineers is critical to the success of the business. We pride ourselves on our culture across engineering of engaging in thorough technical design review, operational excellence, and capable incident response and analysis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Affirm runs its workloads on more than 85 Amazon EKS clusters, and the number is growing. The Workload Safety team creates one set of standards for how workloads are configured and run, so Affirm can grow globally and still meet its availability and latency SLOs. The team identifies the industry best practices Affirm needs, drives their adoption across every engineering team on EKS, and enforces them through policy and automation so new workloads comply by default.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;As a senior engineer on the team, you will help set its roadmap, decide which standards matter most, and build a repeatable way to take each standard from research to enforcement across the fleet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#262626&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Define and evolve workload safety standards for Affirm&#39;s EKS fleet, such as CPU and memory settings, workload isolation and placement, tolerance for disruption, graceful termination to name a few&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Own each standard end to end: research and prototyping, white-glove onboarding for early adopters, self-service guidance for everyone else, and automation and policy guardrails that keep every workload compliant from day one&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Lead cross-team initiatives from design through fleet-wide rollout, mentor other engineers, and set a high bar for design, code review, and operational readiness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Isolate workloads by criticality and resource profile so one misbehaving workload cannot degrade critical paths such as checkout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Fix stuck workloads and node lifecycle problems, such as pods that ignore termination signals, pod disruption budgets that block node cycling, and Karpenter timeouts that prevent bin packing and the removal of excess capacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Determine the safe operating limits of each cluster (pod count, node count, API server request volume), keep clusters within them, and develop control plane scaling patterns for bursty workloads such as scheduled batch jobs and large deployments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Analyze workload resource profiles across the fleet (CPU, memory, disk, network) to guide EC2 instance type strategy, and automate that analysis as workloads change&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Measure each standard&#39;s impact on availability, latency, risk, and cost, and use the results to prioritize the roadmap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Participate in on-call for Kubernetes runtime issues across the fleet, and turn recurring failure patterns into roadmap items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Work closely with the teams that run services, batch jobs, and ML workloads on EKS, and with the deployment, capacity, and SRE teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Keep up with new best practices from the Kubernetes community and adapt them to Affirm&#39;s needs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#262626&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;What we look for&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;5+ years of experience running Kubernetes in production at scale, ideally Amazon EKS across many clusters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Deep understanding of Kubernetes resource management and scheduling: requests and limits, OOM and CPU throttling behavior, affinity and anti-affinity, taints and tolerations, and topology spread constraints&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Solid grasp of the pod lifecycle and disruption management, including graceful termination, pod disruption budgets, and node draining&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Experience enforcing configuration standards through admission control and policy-as-code (for example, OPA Gatekeeper or Kyverno)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Proficiency in Go or Python, including building production infrastructure software such as Kubernetes controllers, operators, or admission webhooks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Strong production debugging skills and a demonstrated ability to turn recurring incidents into systemic fixes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Track record of leading technical initiatives across multiple teams, driving adoption of shared standards, and mentoring other engineers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Experience quantifying the impact of infrastructure changes on availability, latency, and cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;color:#24292f !important&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#24292f&quot;&gt;Strong written communication, including standards and guidance that teams can adopt on their own&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;[**THE BELOW ARE INSTRUCTIONS FOR RECRUITERS.*** &lt;/b&gt;WHEN COPYING INTO WORKDAY, INCLUDE &lt;b&gt;ALL&lt;/b&gt; OF THE TEXT BELOW.&lt;b&gt;DO NOT DELETE OR FILL OUT ANY OF THE INFORMATION BELOW.&lt;/b&gt;]&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;[DELETE IF NOT APPLICABLE TO ROLE] For U.S. non-variable roles use the template below:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base Pay Grade -&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade -&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;br&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: $X - $X&lt;br&gt;USA base pay range (all other U.S. states) per year: $X - $X&lt;br&gt;[DELETE IF NOT APPLICABLE TO ROLE] For U.S. variable roles use the template below:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base Pay Grade -&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade -&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;br&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, which includes the annual base pay and the sales incentive target.&lt;br&gt;USA On Target Earnings (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: $X - $X&lt;br&gt;USA On Target Earnings (all other U.S. states) per year: $X - $X&lt;br&gt;[DELETE IF NOT APPLICABLE TO ROLE] For CAN/GBR roles use the template below:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base Pay Grade -&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade -&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills. [IF APPLICABLE] For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, which includes the annual base pay and the sales incentive target.&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents). In addition, the employees may be eligible for equity rewards offered by Affirm Holdings, Inc. (parent company).&lt;br&gt;(CHOOSE ONE - CAN or GBR) base pay range per year: $X - $X&lt;br&gt;[DELETE IF NOT APPLICABLE TO ROLE] For POL roles use the template below:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;We believe the people building honest financial products at Affirm should share in its success. That&#39;s why our total rewards are designed to support your health, growth, financial well-being, and future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In service of our mission, we reward employees through a combination of base pay, equity (from parent company), and comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Base Pay Grade – N&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;$XXX-$XXX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Base pay ranges and placement within those ranges are determined based on several factors, including role, experience, and job-related skills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;In addition to base pay, all employees in this role are eligible to receive equity from the parent company each year. This means as Affirm’s parent company grows, employees have the opportunity to share in that growth financially.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Equity Grade – 4 (awarded in US Dollars)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Affirm Holdings, Inc. Equity Grade example&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Equity grade: 2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;New hire equity: $16,000-$24,000&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Annual Refresh: $5,000&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reward equity: $0-$75,000&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Affirm also provides flexible spending wallets to all employees for technology and wellbeing related needs, which are reimbursable up to 1390 zł per month.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;In addition to your compensation, our comprehensive benefits are designed to support you and the people who matter most. Benefits include:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Competitive paid time off, paid public holidays, and additional paid Away Days to rest and recharge.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive private healthcare through Lux Med&#39;s Platinum package.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A MultiSport card to support your health and well-being.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Learning and development programs to help you grow professionally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Family healthcare support through Maven and parental leave support through Parentaly.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Mental well-being support through Lyra, including up to 12 confidential counseling or coaching sessions each year for you and your household members.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Financial well-being support through Northstar, with unlimited access to Certified Financial Advisors and planning tools at no cost to you.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) that foster connection and inclusion.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Eligibility for creative tax benefits, subject to applicable law, role, and company policy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Location - Remote Poland&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;The majority of our roles can be located anywhere in Poland.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;**This job description is not a contractual document, and is not intended to have binding force.**&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;LI-Remote&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;[DELETE IF NOT APPLICABLE TO ROLE] For ESP roles use the template below:&lt;br&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base Pay Grade -&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade -&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents). In addition, the employees may be eligible for equity rewards offered by Affirm Holdings, Inc. (parent company).&lt;br&gt;ESP base pay range per year: €X - €X&lt;br&gt;Additional benefits include:&lt;br&gt;• Flexible Spending Wallets for tech, food and lifestyle&lt;br&gt;• Away Days - wellness days to take off work and recharge&lt;br&gt;• Learning &amp;amp; Development programs&lt;br&gt;• Parental benefits&lt;br&gt;• Employee Resource &amp;amp; Community Groups&lt;br&gt;[ONLY KEEP THIS IF WE DO NOT SPONSOR THE ROLE] Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;br&gt;[REMOVE IF POSTING IS NOT REMOTE] LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt; &lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
