&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced, motivated Senior Technical Program Manager to oversee high visibility planning programs for our teams and help streamline our processes for building and delivering great customer and merchant products. As our products scale in complexity to meet our accelerating business and expanding product lines, our business and technology process management practices need to scale with it. In this role, you will work closely with engineering, product, analytics, and other cross-functional teams to align efforts with goals, identify opportunities for improvement, and drive change initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive complex, multi-disciplinary, and highly visible transformation &amp;amp; operational programs in service of our team’s mission to deliver honest financial products that improve lives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders across the company to drive alignment on strategy, priorities, and key decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement lean processes and drive towards better ways of working to realize value from planning, ask questions that clarify priorities and push the team to be effective, and build a culture of continuous iteration and improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and run data-driven operational frameworks to view portfolio performance against OKRs, accelerate value realization by enabling right investment decisions, influence and train teams on more effective ways of working, and create excitement around change to increase adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop communication strategies to ensure critical information flows seamlessly across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams to plan change requirements, identify risks, manage dependencies, and establish tools and forums to drive clarity and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and distill needs, experiment with new ideas to address systemic inefficiencies and bring transparency, visibility, alignment, and promote accountability across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;8 years of proven experience managing programs, processes, and change management in a technology-focused environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Strong technical background with a deep understanding of software development processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Organized and strategic approach to collaborating across multi-disciplinary teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Obsesses over getting the details right but knows how to make tradeoff decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Strong stakeholder management with Product, Engineering, Design, Analytics, and other cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Track record of successfully implementing frameworks at scale and building relationships in a remote friendly culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Excellent communication, interpersonal, and consulting skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Passion and drive to change consumer finance for the better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Prior experience in FinTech, Payments or Commerce is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay Grade - L&lt;br&gt;Equity Grade - 6&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: $165,000 - $225,000&lt;br&gt;USA base pay range (all other U.S. states) per year: $146,000 - $206,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and consent to the use of your personal information as described.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;About the role&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Affirm is seeking an experienced, quota-carrying Account Executive to own the full sales cycle for complex, high-growth merchants across the upper SMB and Mid-Market segment. This portfolio includes merchants with up to $300M in total annual sales and requires a seller who can operate as the general manager of a territory, create demand, engage executive decision-makers, build a quantified business case, structure a compelling commercial solution, and lead the opportunity through contract and launch.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;The Account Executive is accountable for new merchant acquisition and the long-term quality of each partnership. The role translates merchant priorities into solutions across Affirm&#39;s products and capabilities, while aligning internal stakeholders across Sales, Merchant Pricing, Product, Partnerships, Risk, Legal, Operations, Implementation, and Merchant Success. Success requires strategic prospecting, strong financial and commercial judgment, fluency in technical and operational requirements, and the ability to create momentum across complex buying groups.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What you will do&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Own a defined territory and revenue plan.&lt;/b&gt; Operate as the general manager of a portfolio that includes complex, high-growth merchants with up to $300M in total annual sales. Develop the account strategy, prioritization model, pipeline plan, and execution cadence required to achieve signed GMV and revenue targets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Generate and develop net-new pipeline.&lt;/b&gt; Research priority merchants, identify relevant business and market triggers, and use targeted outbound, partner channels, events, referrals, and internal resources to create qualified opportunities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lead executive discovery.&lt;/b&gt; Engage founders, C-suite executives, and senior leaders across Finance, E-commerce, Product, Technology, Operations, and Marketing to understand strategic priorities, operating constraints, customer economics, and decision criteria.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Set the strategy for complex opportunities.&lt;/b&gt; Independently determine the account plan, stakeholder engagement strategy, competitive positioning, internal resource requirements, negotiation posture, and path to close for each opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Build quantified business cases.&lt;/b&gt; Translate merchant data and objectives into clear recommendations supported by expected conversion, average order value, customer acquisition, repeat purchase, GMV, revenue, unit economics, and operational impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Design the merchant solution.&lt;/b&gt; Partner with Sales Engineering and Onboarding to define the appropriate product configuration, integration path, rollout strategy, and customer experience. Lead opportunities that may require customized payment configurations, e-commerce platform integrations, technical solutioning, or multi-entity implementation planning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Navigate complex buying processes.&lt;/b&gt; Build champions, map stakeholders, align economic buyers and technical evaluators, manage procurement, security, legal, and risk requirements, and establish a mutual action plan through decision and signature.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lead commercial negotiations.&lt;/b&gt; Develop deal strategy, position differentiated value, handle objections, and negotiate pricing, terms, and partnership structure. Evaluate merchant requirements against expected GMV, revenue, unit economics, implementation complexity, and risk while protecting Affirm’s long-term financial interests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Develop recommendations for non-standard partnerships.&lt;/b&gt; Use sound commercial judgment to structure and present recommendations involving custom pricing, contractual terms, product requirements, implementation investments, or other exceptions requiring internal approval.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lead cross-functional deal teams.&lt;/b&gt; Lead virtual teams without direct authority by establishing clear owners, operating cadence, decision points, escalation paths, and timelines across Partnerships, Risk, Legal, Implementation, and Merchant Pricing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Own the path from signature to launch.&lt;/b&gt; Remain accountable for a successful handoff and project-manage critical launch dependencies so signed merchants progress efficiently toward integration and go-live.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Maintain forecast and operating discipline.&lt;/b&gt; Keep Salesforce current, accurately assess deal stage and material risk, provide reliable weekly and quarterly forecasts, and communicate changes early with a clear recovery plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Represent the market internally.&lt;/b&gt; Bring structured merchant, industry, and competitive insights to product and business partners, identify recurring barriers, and influence scalable improvements to Affirm’s products and go-to-market motion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Raise team performance.&lt;/b&gt; Share effective account strategies, executive messaging, business cases, and deal practices. Contribute to a high-accountability culture focused on customer value, commercial discipline, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What success looks like&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Revenue and GMV attainment.&lt;/b&gt; Consistently meet or exceed signed annualized estimated GMV and revenue goals across a portfolio of upper-SMB and Mid-Market merchants.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pipeline creation and quality.&lt;/b&gt; Maintain sufficient qualified coverage through self-generated and partner-supported pipeline, supported by clear account prioritization, stakeholder access, and actionable next steps.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Conversion and velocity.&lt;/b&gt; Advance qualified opportunities with healthy win rates, disciplined stage progression, and sales cycles appropriate to the size and complexity of each partnership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Commercial quality.&lt;/b&gt; Structure partnerships that balance merchant value with Affirm’s revenue, unit economics, implementation requirements, and risk considerations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Forecast accuracy.&lt;/b&gt; Provide a reliable view of expected outcomes, material risks, decision criteria, and timing based on evidence and confirmed buyer commitments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Executive engagement.&lt;/b&gt; Establish credibility with senior decision-makers, build effective internal champions, and maintain alignment across complex buying groups.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Launch quality.&lt;/b&gt; Ensure signed merchants transition effectively into implementation and progress toward go-live with aligned scope, owners, technical requirements, and timelines.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cross-functional leadership.&lt;/b&gt; Create clarity, accountability, and momentum across internal teams while representing both merchant needs and Affirm’s business requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Organizational impact.&lt;/b&gt; Surface recurring merchant and market insights that improve product capabilities, remove operating barriers, and strengthen Affirm’s broader go-to-market execution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What we look for&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;4 or more years of quota-carrying, full-cycle closing experience in B2B SaaS, fintech, payments, e-commerce, or another complex technology environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;A demonstrated record of meeting or exceeding revenue targets and creating self-sourced pipeline in a new-logo acquisition role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles and building relationships with executive and functional decision-makers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Strong consultative discovery, objection handling, negotiation, and closing skills, including the ability to establish a clear decision process and mutual action plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Ability to analyze merchant and market data, develop a quantified business case, and communicate financial and strategic value with credibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Experience coordinating legal, risk, technical, pricing, operational, and implementation stakeholders to resolve barriers and close business.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Strong territory planning, pipeline management, CRM discipline, and forecasting capabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, including executive presentations and concise internal updates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;High ownership, sound judgment, resilience, and the ability to operate effectively in a fast-changing environment with multiple priorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Preferred experience&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Experience selling payment, lending, commerce, financial software, or other solutions that require technical integration and commercial structuring.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Familiarity with e-commerce platforms, APIs, payment flows, implementation requirements, and merchant economics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Experience using a structured sales methodology such as MEDDPICC, Challenger, or Sandler.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Prior experience in business development or another role requiring high-volume prospecting and disciplined pipeline creation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#000000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Role requirements&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Ability to work effectively in a remote environment and collaborate across functions and time zones.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Ability to travel periodically for merchant meetings, industry events, and internal team sessions as business needs require.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#1f2937&quot;&gt;Authorization to work in the United States without current or future visa sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
